  "@type": "Note",
  "@id": "note:notion-306",
  "title": "Back Cover Feedback",
  "status": "reviewing",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "b-1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 1,
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Back Cover Feedback"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-2",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "![image.png](Back%20Cover%20Feedback/image.png)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-3",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "**Stephen:**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-4",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> A couple thoughts for Monday from looking through everything"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-5",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Front Cover"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-6",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "(1) I want to make sure we have a 12.6\" x 10.4\" version that's ready to go"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-7",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "(2) the front and back covers are going to be covered in a soft touch finish that gives it a certain tactile feel. will make things like coloring in on the covers impossible (but there will be opportunities on the inside). for the front cover, there's an opportunity to make certain things \"pop\" by working with the sfx team. are there any items on the front cover you would want accentuated? i'm specifically thinking of either accentuating the \"Black Mythology Magazine\" wording and the hands OR accentuating the sun and the \"Vol. 1: Take off the Mask!\" to add emphasis"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-8",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-9",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> [Sample User](https://www.figma.com/files/null/user/720176019422386305) re: back cover"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-12",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> (1) I'm absolutely blown away with the design. how do you feel?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> (2) i prefer the logo shape used in the other pieces than the one in this iteration. curious: how does the logo look if the \"sun\" and \"guy\" are gray, and the negative space is orange?"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> (3) i lovee your sisters take on it. i still prefer black background and our gray fill, while adding bursts of color to make sure its complimentary to/evolving tonally out of the front cover. some of my favorite uses of color on her take of the cover, are (a) coloring in some of the flower petals in the top right; (b) adding color fills to each of the moons on the left side; (c) the outlines of the bubbles on the bottom left and the ripples near our character; (d) adding fills fills to the vine on the bottom left; (e) giving the lady on the bottom right color so it can be interpreted more broadly than  an interracial situation; (f) adding fills to the sub-roots on the right side! Def want you to do what you think makes sense. **after Monday, I'm prepared to run with whatever next iteration you bring me**"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "> (4) i want to flip everything 180 degrees so that the logo occupies the outside of the back cover instead of the inside"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "b-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ">"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}